WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:04.960
Deadpool 2 is finally here, and it left fans
with more than just a stitch in their sides

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.279
- it also left them with a lot of questions.

00:00:07.279 --> 00:00:11.370
Sure, continuity and logic aren't exactly
important in a Deadpool movie, but there are

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:16.379
still some questions we'd love to have answered
even if those answers have absolutely no meaning.

00:00:16.379 --> 00:00:20.509
So grab your stack of X-Force comic books,
button up your 501's, and get ready for a

00:00:20.509 --> 00:00:24.890
bumpy ride, because there's a high wind advisory
in effect for the rest of this spoiler-filled

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:29.270
look at the biggest unanswered questions in
Deadpool 2.

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:30.539
Where ARE the other X-Men?

00:00:30.539 --> 00:00:31.619
"It's a big house.

00:00:31.619 --> 00:00:33.380
It's funny that I only ever see two of you.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:36.650
It's almost like the studio couldn't afford
another X-Man."

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:40.540
Ryan Reynolds and the rest of the Deadpool
gang have made a lot of hay over the fact

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:44.650
that the only X-Men who appear in the two
Deadpool movies are Colossus and Negasonic

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:45.650
Teenage Warhead.

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:49.900
While it was just a wink and nod one-liner
in the first film, this time around, the rest

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:54.980
of the team actually makes a hilarious cameo,
deliberately avoiding Deadpool because...

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:56.300
well, wouldn't you?

00:00:56.300 --> 00:01:00.980
As funny as that was, though, we have to ask:
where exactly are the rest of the X-Men during

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:03.540
the climactic final fight against Juggernaut?

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:07.320
One of the most dangerous mutant menaces in
the world is attacking an orphanage filled

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:09.310
with vulnerable mutant children.

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:12.280
This is the entire reason the X-Men exist
in the first place.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:16.600
And yet, the only ones who bother to show
up are, you guessed it, Colossus and Negasonic

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.570
Teenage Warhead, along with her new girlfriend,
Yukio.

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:23.670
What else could possibly be going on that's
so important Wolverine, Storm, Beast, and

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:25.840
the rest of the team couldn't be bothered
to make an appearance?

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:28.520
Of course, they aren't quite the same without
Hugh Jackman…

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:34.180
"I'm Wolverineeeeeeeeeee.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:37.960
Claw Drop."

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:40.480
What happened to the rest of X-Force?

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:44.900
Arguably the funniest part in Deadpool 2 is
the amazing sequence where the newly formed

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:49.500
X-Force tries to parachute down to attack
the convoy carrying Russell, only for almost

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:54.820
every single one of them to be horribly - and
hilariously - killed off in graphic and preposterous

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:55.820
ways.

00:01:55.820 --> 00:02:00.070
Saddest of all, of course, is the death of
gregarious everyman Peter thanks to acid vomit

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:02.810
taking out one of his arms - which kinda sucks.

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:07.440
Luckily, during the end credits scene, Deadpool
uses Cable's time machine to go back in time

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:09.709
and change events so Peter is saved.

00:02:09.709 --> 00:02:12.849
Which begs the question: what happened to
the rest of X-Force?

00:02:12.849 --> 00:02:15.870
Did Deadpool bother to save the lives of the
rest of the team he assembled?

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:17.939
Or did he only save Peter?

00:02:17.939 --> 00:02:21.890
We never find out, though his comment about
how nobody liked Shatterstar suggests at least

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:25.340
one member of the team might not be back for
Deadpool 3.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:26.820
"X-Force!"

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:29.010
What's the deal with Cable?

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:31.590
In the comics, Cable has a lot going on.

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:35.459
He's actually from our time period, sent to
the future to save him from the techno-virus

00:02:35.459 --> 00:02:37.639
that is slowly turning him into a robot.

00:02:37.639 --> 00:02:42.360
He's also the son of Cyclops and Jean Grey's
evil clone, and usually uses his inherited

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:45.819
telepathic and telekinetic abilities to keep
the virus in check.

00:02:45.819 --> 00:02:51.200
Oh, and he comes back from the future to protect
the prophesied mutant messiah, Hope, who he

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:52.840
adopts as his daughter.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:53.840
"I'm Cable.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:54.840
And I'm from the future.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:56.450
And I like blowing s--- up."

00:02:56.450 --> 00:02:59.900
So, like... is any of that at all happening
in the movies?

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:01.799
Is he still Scott and Jean's son?

00:03:01.799 --> 00:03:03.829
Is Hope an adopted mutant messiah?

00:03:03.829 --> 00:03:06.780
Does he have the technovirus, or is that just
a robot arm?

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:08.010
Does he have mutant powers?

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:13.150
At several points in Deadpool 2 his weapons
fly across the room to him - is that telekinesis,

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:15.540
or some kind of technological gadget?

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:18.799
In short, we know almost nothing about the
movie version of Cable.

00:03:18.799 --> 00:03:23.159
Here's hoping we get to know a lot more about
him in the future - no pun intended.

00:03:23.159 --> 00:03:25.379
Is Vanessa actually Death?

00:03:25.379 --> 00:03:28.719
So… is Vanessa actually the avatar of Death?

00:03:28.719 --> 00:03:30.010
Bear with us on this one.

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:34.379
In the first Deadpool film, Wade Wilson has
a super healing factor that even kept him

00:03:34.379 --> 00:03:36.890
from dying when he was stabbed through the
brain.

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:37.890
That's pretty powerful.

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:41.840
But in Deadpool 2, his power levels seem to
be cranked up more than a few notches.

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:46.140
In fact, he completely blows himself apart
in the opening sequence, with his head flying

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:49.760
off and all his limbs going every direction,
only to get pieced back together.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:54.529
In effect, Deadpool is now immortal, something
he mentions several times in the film, claiming

00:03:54.529 --> 00:03:55.909
he just can't die.

00:03:55.909 --> 00:03:59.300
This is actually true in the comics, where
Wade falls in love with Death, who takes the

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:00.689
form of a beautiful woman.

00:04:00.689 --> 00:04:04.180
Death has a jealous ex, though, who you might
know: Thanos.

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:08.959
He curses Deadpool with immortality so that
Wade and Death can never be together, only

00:04:08.959 --> 00:04:13.159
meeting occasionally in brief flashes of the
afterlife when he is literally on death's

00:04:13.159 --> 00:04:17.310
door - just to be yanked back to life no matter
how hard he tries.

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:21.180
That sounds a whole lot like the relationship
Wade and Vanessa have throughout Deadpool

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:23.710
2 after she is killed in the opening sequence.

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:26.990
Sure, he eventually brings her back to life
during the end credits sequence.

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:31.030
But still, we have to wonder if Vanessa is
actually Death, which would explain why he

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:35.340
can't die, why he sees her when he's close
to dying, and even why he got cancer as soon

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:37.240
as they started a relationship.

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:38.409
Hmm!

00:04:38.409 --> 00:04:40.150
Will there be a Deadpool 3?

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:44.940
Finally, the big question on everyone's mind:
will there even be a Deadpool 3?

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:49.389
With Deadpool 2 set to become another box
office smash, it's a no brainer that the folks

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:51.840
at 20th Century Fox would love to make another
one.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:54.070
And fans are certainly clamoring for it.

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:58.060
But Ryan Reynolds recently told Entertainment
Weekly that he's not so sure.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:04:59.060
Why?

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:02.520
Well, for the best of reasons: he's not convinced
it would be a good story, saying.

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:06.250
"In order for [Deadpool] to function properly
within his own universe, you need to take

00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:07.590
everything away from him.

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:09.509
I don't think that you can keep doing that.

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:12.189
I do see him as being a part of X-Force, obviously.

00:05:12.189 --> 00:05:14.620
I would love to see him in a team-up sort
of thing.

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:18.699
[...] I just think if you're going to do another
Deadpool solo film, you've got to really,

00:05:18.699 --> 00:05:22.810
like, get that budget down to nothing and
just swing for the fences, and break all kinds

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:25.750
of weird barriers, and do stuff that no one
else can do."

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:29.520
Luckily, there's an X-Force film currently
in development, and the end of the film certainly

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:31.540
seems to set up a team spinoff.

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:35.909
So one way or another, there looks to be more
Deadpool in our future - and hopefully, more

00:05:35.909 --> 00:05:36.909
Peter too.

00:05:36.909 --> 00:05:37.909
That guy is the best.

00:05:37.909 --> 00:05:41.139
"As it turns out, we're looking for someone
with Diabetes."

00:05:41.139 --> 00:05:42.139
"Peter's your man."

00:05:42.139 --> 00:05:43.139
Thanks for watching!

00:05:43.139 --> 00:05:45.639
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:45.639 --> 00:05:48.210
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

